From: Kotesh Murugan <koteshlost@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] dualopend: handle NULL from psbt_append_output

Follow-up to 0002. The two dualopend call-sites that build the funding
PSBT must surface NULL from psbt_append_output:

  - the user-output path (line ~1993): an attacker-supplied output is a
    peer-protocol error and should send tx_abort, not crash.

  - the funding-output path (line ~2778): if libwally rejects our own
    funding output, that's an internal invariant violation and we
    status_failed() instead of dereferencing NULL.

---
 openingd/dualopend.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/openingd/dualopend.c b/openingd/dualopend.c
--- a/openingd/dualopend.c
+++ b/openingd/dualopend.c
@@ -1991,6 +1991,10 @@ static bool run_tx_interactive(struct state *state,
 			}

 			out = psbt_append_output(psbt, scriptpubkey, amt);
+			if (!out) {
+				open_abort(state, "Output rejected by PSBT");
+				return false;
+			}
 			psbt_output_set_serial_id(psbt, out, serial_id);
 			break;
 		}
@@ -2778,6 +2782,9 @@ static void add_funding_output(struct tx_state *tx_state,
 	funding_out = psbt_append_output(tx_state->psbt,
 					 scriptpubkey_p2wsh(tmpctx, wscript),
 					 total);
+	if (!funding_out)
+		status_failed(STATUS_FAIL_INTERNAL_ERROR,
+			      "funding output rejected by PSBT");

 	/* Add a serial_id for this output */
 	tx_state->funding_serial = psbt_new_input_serial(tx_state->psbt,
